Recommends: mangohud, gamemode, gamescope, wl-clipboard, python3-pystray, python3-cairo
Suggests: gpu-screen-recorder
Description: One-switch performance helper for Linux gaming
 Detects a game launching, tunes the CPU governor, process priority,
 compositor and power limits, and reverts them cleanly on exit - then
 watches thermals, frame rate and the Proton log and turns a problem into
 a plain-language report.
 .
 An unprivileged systemd --user daemon does the work; a small polkit-gated
 root helper performs the handful of privileged sysfs writes.
